  "summary": "Oak Park village trustee Derek Eder recaps his major 2025 board votes, including a 5-2 vote to cancel the village's Flock Safety contract and deactivate eight ALPR cameras due to concerns about data sharing with ICE and Texas anti-abortion enforcement. He also covers the bike plan, ICE-free zone ordinance, and 2026 budget.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "I voted along with the 5-2 majority to cancel our contract with Flock Safety and deactivate the eight Automatic License Plate Reader (ALPR) cameras that have been operating in our community since 2022.",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock's willingness to share and sell access to our residents' data to the Trump Administration, ICE, and Texas police enforcing anti-abortion laws, made this technology too dangerous",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    }
  ],
